sequenceDiagram
  %% Decided: ADR 0248 (2026-11-07): a withdrawal publishes the whole private DNS once, through the shared `dns-publish` child, after the Node's own files.
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the Gateway holds each Route-serving Node from admission to the terminal state; a second Route write on it waits (docs/reference/routes.md#coordinate-publication).
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run, official cfgmgmt behaviors and SSH argv commands. docs/reference/routes.md#remove-a-route.
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the Node work of the site child is one Ansible phase (see route:create).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:destroy
  %% kind: route.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Route Nodes<br/>workload · Router
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>private DNS
  CLI->>GW: route:destroy ROUTE
  Note over GW: Guard, capture placements<br/>Route unchanged
  %%> Replacement that never activated:
  %%> - the run also restores the old domain's URL and DNS; the replaced Route stays
  Note over GW: Hold the Route Nodes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - holds each Node that serves this Route's site (Caddy and PHP) from admission to the terminal state
  %%> - a second Route write on one of those Nodes waits (task status `waiting`) and starts when the Node is free, oldest first
  %%> Not held:
  %%> - the DNS Node: every publication writes the whole private DNS and the newest revision wins, so two publications cannot lose each other's change
  %%> Limit:
  %%> - two Route writes on one Node run one after the other, so each waits for the other's whole run
  %%> - a newer write waits behind an older waiting one that shares a Node, and a waiting write can be cancelled
  %%> - a timed-out write keeps its Nodes until Swamp confirms that its run stopped, or for 15 minutes
  %%> - task provision and cancel, instance:register and the Cluster Router writes hold the Nodes for their Route-publish step only, through the `route-hold` call
  %%> - a task that waits starts from the Node's live files; a site block that matches none of its captured states still stops it with `owned_revision_conflict`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-route-removal
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  opt --offline
    SW->>N: Check each Node answers<br/>@swamp/ssh · true
    %%> When:
    %%> - a Node that does not answer is skipped and keeps its residue for `node:converge`; the VPN Node is never skipped
  end
  opt domain outside the TLD
    SW->>V: Remove private DNS<br/>child dns-publish
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the shared publication confirms every member and completes its durable 31-second grace before site withdrawal
  end
  SW->>N: Withdraw site, remove cert<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file absent
  opt development targets
    SW->>N: Converge PHP-FPM pools<br/>child route-create-site · Ansible
  end
  opt Cluster-scoped or public
    SW->>N: Remove unused LAN rules<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall absent
  end
  SW->>N: Check nothing is left<br/>cfgmgmt check · native assert
  alt every step succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event + outputs
    Note over GW: Delete the Route record<br/>residue per skipped Node
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Record the failure<br/>Route unchanged
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task carries the failed step; the Route stays as it was, because a failed Route would render no site
    %%> On the Nodes:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after the fix; every step runs again from the start
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
